PR title: feat(yellow-agy): delegate lifecycle — worktrees, journal, snapshots, collect
PR description:
## Summary

- Adds the yellow-agy run lifecycle on top of the adapter core (#1607): worktree create/remove, a run journal with a single-run claim, pre-turn snapshots and partial-edit reset, and `collect`, which captures commits plus uncommitted changes as a patch. agy itself never runs git.
- Every host git call goes through `HostExec`: scrubbed env, the shared `hookConfig` overrides, the exec-only WSL bridge form, and the repo's filter drivers discovered fresh before each call (`git config --name-only --get-regexp '^filter\.'` → `filterDriverNames`). agy turns get the same driver list through `HostExec.filterDrivers`.
- Still library-only: no commands, CLI or routing yet. Those land in PR C.

## Stack context

PR B of three. It sits on `main` now that PR A (#1607, adapter core) has merged. PR C will add the quota gate, grants/authorize, the CLI, `/agy:*` commands, the MCP preflight and `/linear:delegate` routing.

## Test plan

- `pnpm --filter yellow-agy run typecheck` (src + tests): clean
- `pnpm vitest run` in `plugins/yellow-agy`: 137 passed. These include real-git tests showing that a configured filter driver doesn't run through `createHostExec`.
- `pnpm validate:schemas`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck` at the root: pass
- No real agy run. Real runs happen only on the owner's PC with their go-ahead.

## Solution doc

Skip: the behaviour is specified in `docs/yellow-agy/contract-v0.md`, which this PR updates.

## Notes for reviewers

- Filter discovery reads config only. 
